# Pinned family-mruby/mruby-checkpoint: the mrbgem mruby-checkpoint (doc/checkpoint),
# which writes a running mruby VM's state to an image and resumes it in
# another VM. Same scheme as ASTERISM_PIN:
# - `rake checkpoint:setup` clones this exact commit into
#   vendor/mruby-checkpoint (gitignored); `rake setup` copies the gem
#   (mrbgem.rake, include/, src/) into the picoruby submodule.
# - Public: https clone, CI can fetch it.
# - MRUBY_CHECKPOINT_DIR=<checkout> builds from a working checkout instead
#   (nothing is fetched; rake says when it is not the pinned commit).
# - To update: commit and push its main, put the commit here, run
#   `rake setup` (or any build).
